==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Yule Knight Nurse''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Xmas Spirit Nurse''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Yuletide Nurse's niche is almost non-existent as none of her targeted traits are worth using with her kit. [[Knockback|Knockback]] and [[Slow|Slow]] are notoriously bad vs Aliens since they have many backliners that punishes players for said effect, although she could be used against melee and midranged Aliens with decent results in their absence. Angels are a better target, but that's not saying much, as [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo]] already covers the melee threats, with exceptions being few and far between (such as [[Winged Pigge]]).

==='''True Form'''===
Xmas Spirit Nurse now targets Aku, a trait that actually pairs well with her kit because of how aggressive they can get. However, the lack of [[Shield Piercing]] hinders her to some extent, since Shields Block status effects. Additionally, her lack of Surge Immunity allows [[Death Surge]] damage to build up, even if she's well protected. Because of this, even common Aku threats with Death Surges such as [[Condemned Peng]], [[Fallen Bear]], and [[Sinner Snache]] will deal significant chip damage.

==='''Talents'''===
'''Slow''' is this unit's most notable Talent with the amount of consistency it brings, boosting Slow chance to '''100%''' chance when maxed, which helps in impeding many speedy threats she can outrange.

'''[[Immune to Surge|Surge Immunity]]''' does complement her role against Akus and also makes her a viable choice as an anti-Surge attacker, especially against the likes of [[St. Dober]]. [[Mini Angel Cyclone]] is questionable due to her having a high number of knockbacks and low damage, but this Talent nevertheless allows her to survive for even longer in the very little stages that include any. It also comes in handy if [[Techn-Old Hyena]] generates a Counter Surge, even if this unit's status effects are resisted by said enemy's Sage attributes.

'''[[Immune to Warp|Warp Immunity]]''' is actually a detriment to her performance, since it hinders her ability to reposition.

'''HP Buff''' and '''Attack Buff''' are fairly useless due to Xmas Spirit Nurse being a CC unit. If you wish to improve either of these stats, use [[Catseye]]s before spending any form of NP. Even then, it is ill-advised.

Overall, Xmas Spirit Nurse's Talents do help her turn from a pretty bad seasonal Uber, to a respectable Uber who can be a pretty middle of the pack CC unit. While it is true she needs shield piercing, there are many no-Uber options to help her out.

